From: Alan Shearer
Subject: input_server: keep a touchpad drag moving on a wide contact

Pressing a clickpad makes the contact wider than 7 and can push the
pressure over the normal limit. Those packets were handled as a finger
lift, so a window drag only moved a few pixels.

Accept the full single-finger width and pressure while a button is held.
Taps still use the old check.

---
 src/add-ons/input_server/devices/mouse/movement_maker.cpp | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/input_server/devices/mouse/movement_maker.cpp b/src/add-ons/input_server/devices/mouse/movement_maker.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/input_server/devices/mouse/movement_maker.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/input_server/devices/mouse/movement_maker.cpp
@@ -356,9 +356,17 @@ TouchpadMovement::EventToMovement(const touchpad_movement* _event, mouse_movement* movement,
 			fValidEdgeMotion = false;
 	}
 
+	// A click widens the contact past width 7 and can push pressure over
+	// the normal limit. That was treated as a lift, so the drag stopped
+	// after a few pixels. Keep tracking while a button is held.
+	int32 maxWidth = 7;
+	int32 maxPressure = fSpecs.maxPressure;
+	if (event->buttons != 0) {
+		maxWidth = 15;
+		maxPressure = 256;
+	}
+
 	if (event->zPressure >= fSpecs.minPressure
-		&& event->zPressure < fSpecs.maxPressure
-		&& ((event->fingerWidth >= 4 && event->fingerWidth <= 7)
+		&& event->zPressure < maxPressure
+		&& ((event->fingerWidth >= 4 && event->fingerWidth <= maxWidth)
 			|| two_or_more_fingers(event))
 		&& (event->xPosition != 0 || event->yPosition != 0)) {
 		// The touch pad is in touch with at least one finger
